Subject: rapidcow.org NS change

For a very brief moment you may have seen A records
pointing to rapidcow.org and all its subdomains vanish...
Sorry about that if you thought they're gone ^^; (I think
I had to click some button to tell Cloudflare that I did
change the name servers to them on Namecheap (but I mean,
I hope that your ISP's DNS was smart enough to cache the
DNS records, unlike my uni's CSL that just FORGETS my
domain entirely for like 20 minutes straight... =_=))

Well, I moved to Cloudflare -- as an experiment of sorts.
I'm learning to run BIND9 which is basically why I wanted
to use a DNS server that lets me import zone files directly.

For the few other guys I may stay with Porkbun since they
have (beta) support for zone file imports, and Porkbun is
powered off of Cloudflare too (IIRC?)  But yizx.net and
and yizz.me are going on Cloudflare that's for certain. :)

I think I might also try to see how feasible it is to
update DNS records without all of this happening again!
(After I finish my obligatory homework, well... that
will be this weekend for me and, I'd say... just keep
an eye out for that in the next 15-ish hours ok :x)
